// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/automation/crm-client-workspace.t27 -- one CRM workspace PER CLIENT: a dashboard and a
// conversation thread of the seller ABOUT one client, instead of one thread and one flat list
// for everybody. Written after the owner said (2026-09-13) that every client's chat lands in the
// same place.
// Host: 999-multibots-telegraf apps/vibee-editor -- render: agent_messages.thread (conversation.ts),
//       body.client / ?client= on the four /api/agent routes (routes.ts), clientContextBlock in
//       runAgent (chat.ts), table crm_duet_runs and tool crm_duet_runs (crm-duet-tool.ts), tools
//       crm_client_plan and crm_clients; player: routes /crm/:clientId (dashboard) and
//       /crm/:clientId/chat (client thread), the list at /crm links every row to its client.
// WHAT was measured before this spec (render Postgres, code read 2026-09-13): agent_messages was
//       keyed by telegram_id only -- one thread per person across bot, app and phone; the mini
//       app had one localStorage atom and "new conversation" DELETEd the whole server history;
//       /crm showed three flat panels with no client page; duet runs lived in a process Map and
//       the report went to the owner's Saved Messages -- a redeploy in the middle of a run
//       (duet-mtzsz1la, 2026-09-13 19:41-19:44 +07) lost the run after its first pair.
// WHY a thread key and not a second table: the four routes and both apps already speak
//       agent_messages; a DEFAULT 'self' column keeps every existing row and caller unchanged,
//       and 'client:<id>' gives the seller one thread per client with the client's profile,
//       SOUL status, skills and DM history injected as context (not as instructions).
// Generated: `t27c gen-ts` of this file is vendored into the host as
//       apps/vibee-editor/render/src/spec/crm-client-workspace.gen.ts; the host imports the
//       numbers from there and src/spec/crm-client-workspace.test.ts runs these tests against
//       it (scripts/check-t27-specs.mjs holds both).
// WHY the dashboard reads through /mcp tools and not new REST routes: visibility (owner,
//       seller, stranger) is decided in one place -- the tool gate, before the first DB read
//       (crm-owner-gate.test.ts is the canary); a REST route would be a second gate to keep.
// Claim status: contract and gates written and unit-tested with doubles on both sides; the
//       dashboard being SEEN live by the owner and a duet run SURVIVING a redeploy are shown by
//       the host, not by this file.
// v2 (2026-09-27), from binding v1 to the code: v1's thread_for turned a malformed client id
//       into the seller's own thread, while the host refuses it (400) -- a request about a client
//       never silently becomes a request about oneself; thread_kind says so. The dashboard has 7
//       panels since the story reel (2026-09-26). The Queen's supervision of a client has its
//       own thread beside the agent's ('client:<id>:queen', 2026-09-24), and a specialist called
//       into a client's conversation keeps the CLIENT's memory (2026-09-26).
// v3 (2026-09-27): the Queen's tasks went to the plain assistant whatever specialist the owner had
//       chosen in the client's thread, so a task set for the Blogger was done by someone else,
//       without the Blogger's brief. A task goes to the chosen specialist, or to the assistant
//       when none is chosen (task_goes_to).
// v4 (2026-09-27): the Queen names who does a task, as a handoff names its target: the marker
//       [[task@<agent id>: ...]] with the catalogue's ids listed in her block (OpenAI's handoff
//       tools and LangGraph's supervisor do the same: the model can name only declared agents).
//       A named agent the owner may call gets the task; a name the owner may not call, or one
//       that is no agent, falls back to the chosen specialist, then the assistant -- the task is
//       never lost (task_owner).
// v5 (2026-10-03): the widgets follow the specialist. The owner: the content dashboard shows only
//       when the Blogger is chosen, every other specialist by analogy, and the widgets in one
//       place, a menu on the left. A widget is the client's (shown under anybody) or one
//       specialist's (shown only while that specialist is chosen): the content widget -- the
//       portrait gift and the story reel, on the card "always" since 2026-09-29 -- is the
//       Blogger's; a specialist's templates are its own. All of them sit in one menu in the left
//       column under the client's head, one open at a time, the waiting drafts pinned above it;
//       the Queen keeps the right column and is not a widget (widget_shown, open_after_switch).
//       The same day, the agent sent an old render while the reel panel stood open with a topic
//       and 3 frames: the panel's state never reached it. A client thread's request now carries
//       `widgets` -- the ids shown, the open one, the shown widgets' own state -- checked (known
//       ids, capped values, a capped whole) and put beside the client's brief as context, not
//       instruction. A hidden widget is not reported, and the self thread ignores the field
//       (widget_reported, capped).
// v6 (2026-10-04): client work carries the client's marks. The owner (2026-10-03), on a client's
//       reel that ended with HIS call: "why does it make my CTA and not the client's?" On client
//       work the caller id is the seller's, so a prompt keyed on the caller gave a client's
//       content the house's Blogger brief (the house blog, the house offer, the house triptych)
//       and the seller's 30-day content plan and post voice. A turn is client work when it
//       carries faceOf (a client thread, the duet's buyer) or sellerSweep (an unattended sweep
//       over the seller's leads) -- the only two marks a turn has (content_for). There the
//       Blogger gets the client's brief and the seller's plan stays out; his SOUL still speaks
//       the words sent in his name (the duet). The content is the client's: what the seller said
//       about this client, else the client's profile and plan, else neutral -- never the house's
//       (blogger_brief_is_house, seller_plan_in_prompt). From the review the same day, two more
//       of the house's marks reached client work. A StoryReel rendered for a client with no end
//       card, or a card short of a colour, stood on the house's card -- gold on black, a green
//       button -- because the composition fills whatever is missing with it. On client work her
//       colours are kept, a missing one is the neutral ink or ground that reads against hers, a
//       call with no card stands on the neutral card, and all of it is settled before the twin
//       lookup and the charge (story_card_from). And the prompt told the model on every turn that
//       the bot in speech is the house's; on client work that line is not said
//       (bot_named_in_speech). From the second review the same day, the card was still the
//       house's on the road most client reels take: a reel pressed in the CRM, by the seller or
//       by the client herself, and story_reel for a named lead from the seller's own thread. On
//       that road the turn carries no client mark -- the job runs as its payer, and on her own
//       press the payer is the client -- so the card was left to the composition. Whose reel it
//       is now decides the card, not who is paying for it: a client's when the turn carries a
//       client mark, or when the reel is about a lead who is not the seller (reel_is_clients).
//       The seller's own reel -- his lead is himself, no mark, no lead named -- stays on the
//       house card as given.
// phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module automation::crm_client_workspace {

    pub const KIND : str = "automation";
    pub const ID : str = "crm-client-workspace";
    pub const REPO : str = "999-multibots-telegraf";
    pub const VERSION : u8 = 6;

    // ---- Who ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
    pub const CALLER : str = "seller";  // owner id or a row in tg_sessions (crm-sellers.t27)
    pub const CLIENT_IS : str = "telegram-id";  // numeric, 5..15 digits, never the caller
    pub const CLIENT_ID_MIN_DIGITS : u8 = 5;
    pub const CLIENT_ID_MAX_DIGITS : u8 = 15;

    // ---- The thread -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    pub const THREAD_COLUMN : str = "thread";  // agent_messages.thread
    pub const THREAD_SELF : str = "self";  // DEFAULT: every row and caller from before this spec
    pub const THREAD_CLIENT_PREFIX : str = "client:";  // 'client:<id>' -- the seller's thread about one client
    pub const THREAD_SUPERVISOR_SUFFIX : str = ":queen";  // 'client:<id>:queen' -- the Queen's, beside it
    pub const AGENT_KEEPS_CLIENT_MEMORY : bool = true;  // a specialist in a client's chat writes to 'client:<id>'
    pub const QUEEN_TASK_TO_CHOSEN_SPECIALIST : bool = true;  // v3
    pub const TASK_TO_ASSISTANT : u8 = 0;
    pub const TASK_TO_SPECIALIST : u8 = 1;
    pub const TASK_TO_NAMED : u8 = 2;  // v4
    pub const TASK_MARKER : str = "[[task@";  // [[task@<agent id>: ...]]; plain [[task: ...]] still works
    pub const QUEEN_LISTS_AGENT_IDS : bool = true;  // her block declares the ids she may name
    pub const NAMED_TASK_NEVER_LOST : bool = true;  // an unknown or forbidden name falls back
    // What a request's thread comes to (thread_kind).
    pub const THREAD_KIND_SELF : u8 = 0;  // no client named
    pub const THREAD_KIND_CLIENT : u8 = 1;  // 'client:<id>'
    pub const THREAD_KIND_BAD_CLIENT : u8 = 2;  // HTTP 400: malformed, or the caller's own id
    pub const THREAD_KIND_NOT_SELLER : u8 = 3;  // HTTP 403
    pub const THREAD_PARAM : str = "client";  // body.client on POST, ?client= on GET/DELETE
    pub const ROUTES_WITH_THREAD : u8 = 4;  // chat, history GET, history POST, history DELETE
    pub const DELETE_CLEARS_ONLY_ITS_THREAD : bool = true;  // a client thread never wipes 'self'
    pub const CONTEXT_INJECTED : str = "crm_client_profile+lead_context+widgets";  // as context, not instructions; widgets v5
    pub const GATE_BEFORE_DB : bool = true;  // 400 bad client / 403 not a seller / 400 client == caller

    // ---- The dashboard --------------------------------------------------------------------
    pub const ROUTE_LIST : str = "/crm";
    pub const ROUTE_CLIENT : str = "/crm/:clientId";
    pub const ROUTE_CLIENT_CHAT : str = "/crm/:clientId/chat";
    pub const READS_THROUGH : str = "/mcp";  // tools decide who sees whom; no new REST routes
    pub const PANELS : u8 = 7;  // profile+soul+skills, plan, story reel, duets, touches+stage, media, messages
    pub const UNREACHABLE_SAYS : str = "unavailable";  // never zeros (rule inherited from /crm)
    pub const NEW_READ_TOOLS : u8 = 3;  // crm_clients, crm_client_plan, crm_duet_runs
    pub const DASHBOARD_SENDS_NOTHING_UNASKED : bool = true;  // reads never send; the one sender is the explicit duet control below

    // ---- The start-duet control on /crm/:clientId (#3611) --------------------------------
    pub const DASHBOARD_STARTS_DUET : bool = true;  // calls crm_duet through the same /mcp gate
    pub const DUET_CONTROL_GATE : str = "server";  // owner-only in the tool; the UI shows the refusal text, never guesses the role
    pub const DUET_CONTROL_DEFAULT_DRY_RUN : bool = true;
    pub const DUET_CONTROL_REAL_SEND_CONFIRMS : bool = true;  // dry_run off -> an inline confirm step before the call
    pub const DUET_CONTROL_TURNS_MAX : u8 = 8;
    pub const DUET_CONTROL_TURNS_DEFAULT : u8 = 4;

    // ---- The /crm list (#3611) -------------------------------------------------------------
    pub const LIST_PAID_BADGE : bool = true;  // rows with paid: true carry a badge
    pub const LIST_FILTER : str = "all,clients,leads";  // clients = paid or stage client/winback; leads = the rest
    pub const LIST_SAYS_PAID_UNKNOWN : bool = true;  // paid_known: false is one visible line, not a hidden zero

    // ---- Persisted duet runs ----------------------------------------------------------------
    pub const TABLE_RUNS : str = "crm_duet_runs";
    pub const RUN_PERSISTED_AT : str = "start,turn,finish";
    pub const RUN_LOST_AFTER_MIN : u8 = 30;  // a 'running' row older than this reads as 'lost'
    pub const RUN_LOST_IS_STORED : bool = false;  // derived on read, never written

    // ---- Not claimed ----------------------------------------------------------------------
    pub const DASHBOARD_SEEN_LIVE : bool = true;  // 2026-09-13 ~20:40 +07: /crm, /crm/435572800 and its chat opened by the owner on app.t27.ai after the #2384 deploy (#3608)
    pub const RUN_SURVIVED_REDEPLOY : bool = false;

    // ---- The widgets in the client's chat (v5) ---------------------------------------------
    pub const WIDGETS_FOLLOW_SPECIALIST : bool = true;  // a specialist's widget shows only while it is chosen
    pub const CONTENT_WIDGET_AGENT : str = "blogger";  // the portrait gift and the story reel
    pub const WIDGET_IDS : str = "moves,group,soul,package,plan,history,content,templates";  // the registry, the client's first
    pub const CLIENT_WIDGETS : u8 = 6;  // moves, group, soul, package, plan, history: shown under anybody
    pub const WIDGETS_IN_ONE_MENU : bool = true;  // one menu; no second row of tabs
    pub const WIDGET_MENU_SIDE : str = "left";  // the column under the client's head
    pub const OPEN_WIDGETS : u8 = 1;  // one open at a time
    pub const DRAFTS_PINNED_ABOVE_MENU : bool = true;  // waiting drafts are never behind an entry
    pub const QUEEN_IS_NOT_A_WIDGET : bool = true;  // she keeps the right column
    // What is open after the chosen specialist changes (open_after_switch).
    pub const OPEN_KEEPS : u8 = 0;  // the open widget is still shown: it stays open
    pub const OPEN_SPECIALISTS_FIRST : u8 = 1;  // the newly chosen specialist's first widget opens
    pub const OPEN_FALLS_TO_CLIENT : u8 = 2;  // the open one left with its specialist: a client widget opens

    // ---- What the agent is told about the widgets (v5) -------------------------------------
    pub const AGENT_SEES_WIDGETS : bool = true;
    pub const WIDGET_CONTEXT_PARAM : str = "widgets";  // body.widgets on the chat POST
    pub const WIDGET_CONTEXT_ONLY_IN_CLIENT_THREAD : bool = true;  // the self thread and the Queen's ignore it
    pub const HIDDEN_WIDGET_NOT_REPORTED : bool = true;  // the player does not send it, the render does not read it
    pub const WIDGET_TEXT_MAX_CHARS : u16 = 600;  // one value: the panel's longest field (style) allows 600
    pub const WIDGET_LIST_MAX : u8 = 8;  // ideas, template titles
    pub const WIDGET_CONTEXT_MAX_CHARS : u16 = 4000;  // the whole block; a reel panel filled to every limit fits

    // ---- Client work carries the client's marks (v6) ---------------------------------------
    pub const CLIENT_WORK_MARKS : str = "faceOf,sellerSweep";  // the caller id is the seller's on client work
    pub const CONTENT_IS_CALLERS : u8 = 0;  // the seller's own turn
    pub const CONTENT_IS_CLIENTS : u8 = 1;  // client work: the client's offer, plan and voice
    pub const HOUSE_BRIEF_ON_CLIENT_WORK : bool = false;  // the Blogger's house brief: house blog, offer, triptych
    pub const SELLER_PLAN_ON_CLIENT_WORK : bool = false;  // the seller's 30-day plan and post voice
    pub const SELLER_SOUL_SPEAKS_HIS_OWN_WORDS : bool = true;  // a message sent in his name keeps his voice
    pub const CLIENT_CONTENT_FROM : str = "seller-for-this-client,client-profile,neutral";  // the first that has a value
    pub const CLIENT_STORYREEL_NO_HOUSE_PALETTE : bool = true;  // a client's story reel never stands on the house card
    pub const STORY_CARD_AS_GIVEN : u8 = 0;  // the seller's own turn: the composition's card, the house's when none
    pub const STORY_CARD_HERS : u8 = 1;  // client work with her card: her colours, a missing one neutral
    pub const STORY_CARD_NEUTRAL : u8 = 2;  // client work, a call and no card: the neutral card
    pub const STORY_CARD_NONE : u8 = 3;  // client work, no call and no card: the pause shows none
    pub const NEUTRAL_CARD_DARK : str = "#1f1f1f";  // the neutral ground, and the ink on a light ground
    pub const NEUTRAL_CARD_LIGHT : str = "#f5f5f5";  // the neutral ink, and the ground under a dark colour
    pub const CLIENT_PROMPT_NO_HOUSE_BOT_NAME : bool = true;  // "the bot in speech is ours" stays off client work
    pub const CLIENT_REEL_IS : str = "client-mark,lead-not-seller";  // whose reel it is, the first that holds
    pub const CLIENT_REEL_ROUTES : str = "client-turn,crm-template,story-reel-for-lead";  // every road to her reel
    pub const CLIENT_REEL_BY_PAYER : bool = false;  // her own press makes her the payer; the reel is hers all the same

    // What a request's thread comes to. A named client that is malformed, or is the caller,
    // is refused: a request about somebody never quietly becomes a request about oneself.
    fn thread_kind(client_named: bool, client_digits: u8, is_caller: bool, is_seller: bool) -> u8 {
        if !client_named {
            return THREAD_KIND_SELF;
        }
        let malformed = client_digits < CLIENT_ID_MIN_DIGITS || client_digits > CLIENT_ID_MAX_DIGITS;
        if malformed || is_caller {
            return THREAD_KIND_BAD_CLIENT;
        }
        if !is_seller {
            return THREAD_KIND_NOT_SELLER;
        }
        return THREAD_KIND_CLIENT;
    }

    // A request is refused before any read when the client is malformed, is the caller, or the caller is no seller.
    fn refused_before_db(client_digits: u8, is_caller: bool, is_seller: bool) -> bool {
        let malformed = client_digits < CLIENT_ID_MIN_DIGITS || client_digits > CLIENT_ID_MAX_DIGITS;
        return malformed || is_caller || !is_seller;
    }

    // Who does a task the Queen set: the specialist chosen in the thread, else the assistant.
    fn task_goes_to(specialist_chosen: bool) -> u8 {
        if specialist_chosen {
            return TASK_TO_SPECIALIST;
        }
        return TASK_TO_ASSISTANT;
    }

    // Who does a task the Queen set, v4: the agent she named when the owner may call it, else
    // the specialist chosen in the thread, else the assistant.
    fn task_owner(named_callable: bool, specialist_chosen: bool) -> u8 {
        if named_callable {
            return TASK_TO_NAMED;
        }
        return task_goes_to(specialist_chosen);
    }

    fn run_reads_as_lost(state_running: bool, minutes_since_start: u8) -> bool {
        return state_running && minutes_since_start > RUN_LOST_AFTER_MIN;
    }

    // A widget is shown when it is the client's, or when the specialist it belongs to is chosen.
    fn widget_shown(belongs_to_specialist: bool, owner_is_chosen: bool) -> bool {
        return !belongs_to_specialist || owner_is_chosen;
    }

    // What is open after the chosen specialist changes: the new specialist's own widget when it
    // brings one, else the open widget while it is still shown, else a client widget.
    fn open_after_switch(chosen_has_widgets: bool, open_still_shown: bool) -> u8 {
        if chosen_has_widgets {
            return OPEN_SPECIALISTS_FIRST;
        }
        if open_still_shown {
            return OPEN_KEEPS;
        }
        return OPEN_FALLS_TO_CLIENT;
    }

    // The agent hears of a widget only when the owner sees it, and only in a client's thread.
    fn widget_reported(shown: bool, client_thread: bool) -> bool {
        return shown && client_thread;
    }

    // A value longer than its cap is cut to the cap.
    fn capped(length: u16, cap: u16) -> u16 {
        if length > cap {
            return cap;
        }
        return length;
    }

    // Whose content a turn makes: the client's when it carries either mark, never by the caller id.
    fn content_for(face_of: bool, seller_sweep: bool) -> u8 {
        if face_of || seller_sweep {
            return CONTENT_IS_CLIENTS;
        }
        return CONTENT_IS_CALLERS;
    }

    // The Blogger's house brief is for the seller's own turns only.
    fn blogger_brief_is_house(client_work: bool) -> bool {
        return !client_work;
    }

    // The seller's content plan and post voice go into the prompt on his own turns only.
    fn seller_plan_in_prompt(seller_soul: bool, client_work: bool) -> bool {
        return seller_soul && !client_work;
    }

    // Whose reel a StoryReel is: a client's when the turn carries a client mark, or when the reel
    // is about a lead who is not the seller -- the CRM template, pressed by the seller or by her,
    // and story_reel for a named lead. Who pays is never asked: on her own press she is the payer.
    fn reel_is_clients(client_turn: bool, lead_named: bool, lead_is_seller: bool, lead_is_payer: bool) -> bool {
        return client_turn || (lead_named && !lead_is_seller);
    }

    // The card a StoryReel's pause stands on. On client work the house's card is never left to
    // the composition's defaults: her colours, else neutral; nothing when there is nothing to show.
    fn story_card_from(client_work: bool, card_given: bool, call_given: bool) -> u8 {
        if !client_work {
            return STORY_CARD_AS_GIVEN;
        }
        if card_given {
            return STORY_CARD_HERS;
        }
        if call_given {
            return STORY_CARD_NEUTRAL;
        }
        return STORY_CARD_NONE;
    }

    // The prompt names the house's bot in speech on the seller's own turns only.
    fn bot_named_in_speech(client_work: bool) -> bool {
        return !client_work;
    }

    test "a client thread is separate from the seller's own thread and clearing one keeps the other" {
        assert(thread_kind(false, 0, false, true) == THREAD_KIND_SELF);
        assert(thread_kind(true, 9, false, true) == THREAD_KIND_CLIENT);
        assert(THREAD_SELF == "self");
        assert(THREAD_CLIENT_PREFIX == "client:");
        assert(DELETE_CLEARS_ONLY_ITS_THREAD);
        assert(ROUTES_WITH_THREAD == 4);
    }

    test "a stranger, a malformed id and the caller's own id are refused before the first read" {
        assert(GATE_BEFORE_DB);
        assert(refused_before_db(9, false, false));
        assert(refused_before_db(3, false, true));
        assert(refused_before_db(16, false, true));
        assert(refused_before_db(9, true, true));
        assert(!refused_before_db(9, false, true));
        assert(thread_kind(true, 3, false, true) == THREAD_KIND_BAD_CLIENT);
        assert(thread_kind(true, 16, false, true) == THREAD_KIND_BAD_CLIENT);
        assert(thread_kind(true, 9, true, true) == THREAD_KIND_BAD_CLIENT);
        assert(thread_kind(true, 9, false, false) == THREAD_KIND_NOT_SELLER);
    }

    test "the Queen's thread sits beside the agent's, and a specialist keeps the client's memory" {
        assert(THREAD_SUPERVISOR_SUFFIX == ":queen");
        assert(AGENT_KEEPS_CLIENT_MEMORY);
    }

    test "the Queen's task goes to the specialist chosen in the thread, else to the assistant" {
        assert(QUEEN_TASK_TO_CHOSEN_SPECIALIST);
        assert(task_goes_to(true) == TASK_TO_SPECIALIST);
        assert(task_goes_to(false) == TASK_TO_ASSISTANT);
    }

    test "the Queen may name who does a task; a name the owner cannot call falls back and the task is kept" {
        assert(TASK_MARKER == "[[task@");
        assert(QUEEN_LISTS_AGENT_IDS);
        assert(NAMED_TASK_NEVER_LOST);
        assert(task_owner(true, true) == TASK_TO_NAMED);
        assert(task_owner(true, false) == TASK_TO_NAMED);
        assert(task_owner(false, true) == TASK_TO_SPECIALIST);
        assert(task_owner(false, false) == TASK_TO_ASSISTANT);
    }

    test "the dashboard reads through the tool gate, sends nothing unasked and says unavailable rather than zero" {
        assert(READS_THROUGH == "/mcp");
        assert(DASHBOARD_SENDS_NOTHING_UNASKED);
        assert(DASHBOARD_STARTS_DUET);
        assert(DUET_CONTROL_GATE == "server");
        assert(DUET_CONTROL_DEFAULT_DRY_RUN);
        assert(DUET_CONTROL_REAL_SEND_CONFIRMS);
        assert(DUET_CONTROL_TURNS_DEFAULT <= DUET_CONTROL_TURNS_MAX);
        assert(LIST_PAID_BADGE);
        assert(LIST_FILTER == "all,clients,leads");
        assert(LIST_SAYS_PAID_UNKNOWN);
        assert(UNREACHABLE_SAYS == "unavailable");
        assert(PANELS == 7);
        assert(NEW_READ_TOOLS == 3);
    }

    test "duet runs are written at start, each turn and finish, and a stale running row reads as lost" {
        assert(TABLE_RUNS == "crm_duet_runs");
        assert(RUN_PERSISTED_AT == "start,turn,finish");
        assert(run_reads_as_lost(true, 31));
        assert(!run_reads_as_lost(true, 30));
        assert(!run_reads_as_lost(false, 90));
        assert(!RUN_LOST_IS_STORED);
    }

    test "the client is a telegram id, the caller is a seller, and only the dashboard is claimed live" {
        assert(CLIENT_IS == "telegram-id");
        assert(CALLER == "seller");
        assert(ROUTE_CLIENT == "/crm/:clientId");
        assert(ROUTE_CLIENT_CHAT == "/crm/:clientId/chat");
        assert(DASHBOARD_SEEN_LIVE);
        assert(!RUN_SURVIVED_REDEPLOY);
    }

    test "a client widget shows under any specialist, a specialist's only while it is chosen" {
        assert(WIDGETS_FOLLOW_SPECIALIST);
        assert(widget_shown(false, false));
        assert(widget_shown(false, true));
        assert(widget_shown(true, true));
        assert(!widget_shown(true, false));
        assert(CLIENT_WIDGETS == 6);
    }

    test "the content widget is the Blogger's: absent under the Assistant and under any other specialist" {
        assert(CONTENT_WIDGET_AGENT == "blogger");
        assert(WIDGETS_FOLLOW_SPECIALIST);
        assert(!widget_shown(true, false));
        assert(widget_shown(true, true));
    }

    test "all widgets sit in one menu on the left, one open at a time, the drafts above it, and the Queen is not one of them" {
        assert(WIDGETS_IN_ONE_MENU);
        assert(WIDGET_MENU_SIDE == "left");
        assert(OPEN_WIDGETS == 1);
        assert(DRAFTS_PINNED_ABOVE_MENU);
        assert(QUEEN_IS_NOT_A_WIDGET);
        assert(WIDGET_IDS == "moves,group,soul,package,plan,history,content,templates");
        assert(PANELS == 7);
    }

    test "choosing a specialist opens its widget, and leaving it falls back to a client widget" {
        assert(open_after_switch(true, true) == OPEN_SPECIALISTS_FIRST);
        assert(open_after_switch(true, false) == OPEN_SPECIALISTS_FIRST);
        assert(open_after_switch(false, true) == OPEN_KEEPS);
        assert(open_after_switch(false, false) == OPEN_FALLS_TO_CLIENT);
    }

    test "the agent is told the widgets the owner sees, in a client's thread only, and never a hidden one" {
        assert(AGENT_SEES_WIDGETS);
        assert(WIDGET_CONTEXT_PARAM == "widgets");
        assert(CONTEXT_INJECTED == "crm_client_profile+lead_context+widgets");
        assert(HIDDEN_WIDGET_NOT_REPORTED);
        assert(WIDGET_CONTEXT_ONLY_IN_CLIENT_THREAD);
        assert(widget_reported(true, true));
        assert(!widget_reported(false, true));
        assert(!widget_reported(true, false));
        assert(!widget_reported(false, false));
    }

    test "a widget's values are capped one by one and as a whole" {
        assert(capped(601, WIDGET_TEXT_MAX_CHARS) == WIDGET_TEXT_MAX_CHARS);
        assert(capped(120, WIDGET_TEXT_MAX_CHARS) == 120);
        assert(capped(5000, WIDGET_CONTEXT_MAX_CHARS) == WIDGET_CONTEXT_MAX_CHARS);
        assert(WIDGET_TEXT_MAX_CHARS < WIDGET_CONTEXT_MAX_CHARS);
        assert(WIDGET_LIST_MAX == 8);
    }

    test "work for a client is told by its marks, never by the caller id" {
        assert(CLIENT_WORK_MARKS == "faceOf,sellerSweep");
        assert(content_for(true, false) == CONTENT_IS_CLIENTS);
        assert(content_for(false, true) == CONTENT_IS_CLIENTS);
        assert(content_for(true, true) == CONTENT_IS_CLIENTS);
        assert(content_for(false, false) == CONTENT_IS_CALLERS);
    }

    test "on client work the Blogger gets the client's brief, never the house's" {
        assert(!HOUSE_BRIEF_ON_CLIENT_WORK);
        assert(blogger_brief_is_house(false));
        assert(!blogger_brief_is_house(true));
        assert(CLIENT_CONTENT_FROM == "seller-for-this-client,client-profile,neutral");
    }

    test "on client work the seller's plan and post voice stay out, and his SOUL speaks only his own words" {
        assert(!SELLER_PLAN_ON_CLIENT_WORK);
        assert(SELLER_SOUL_SPEAKS_HIS_OWN_WORDS);
        assert(seller_plan_in_prompt(true, false));
        assert(!seller_plan_in_prompt(true, true));
        assert(!seller_plan_in_prompt(false, false));
        assert(!seller_plan_in_prompt(false, true));
    }

    test "a client's story reel never stands on the house card" {
        assert(CLIENT_STORYREEL_NO_HOUSE_PALETTE);
        assert(story_card_from(false, false, true) == STORY_CARD_AS_GIVEN);
        assert(story_card_from(false, true, false) == STORY_CARD_AS_GIVEN);
        assert(story_card_from(true, true, false) == STORY_CARD_HERS);
        assert(story_card_from(true, true, true) == STORY_CARD_HERS);
        assert(story_card_from(true, false, true) == STORY_CARD_NEUTRAL);
        assert(story_card_from(true, false, false) == STORY_CARD_NONE);
        assert(NEUTRAL_CARD_DARK == "#1f1f1f");
        assert(NEUTRAL_CARD_LIGHT == "#f5f5f5");
    }

    test "a reel about a lead who is not the seller is hers on every road, whoever pays" {
        assert(CLIENT_REEL_IS == "client-mark,lead-not-seller");
        assert(CLIENT_REEL_ROUTES == "client-turn,crm-template,story-reel-for-lead");
        assert(!CLIENT_REEL_BY_PAYER);
        // The CRM template pressed by the seller for her: he pays, the reel is hers.
        assert(reel_is_clients(false, true, false, false));
        // Her own press: she pays, and the reel is still hers.
        assert(reel_is_clients(false, true, false, true));
        // story_reel for a named lead from the seller's own thread.
        assert(reel_is_clients(false, true, false, false));
        // A turn for a client, with or without a lead named.
        assert(reel_is_clients(true, false, false, false));
        assert(reel_is_clients(true, true, false, false));
        // The seller's own reel: his lead is himself, or no lead at all.
        assert(!reel_is_clients(false, true, true, true));
        assert(!reel_is_clients(false, false, false, true));
        // And her reel never stands on the house card, by any road.
        assert(story_card_from(reel_is_clients(false, true, false, true), false, true) == STORY_CARD_NEUTRAL);
        assert(story_card_from(reel_is_clients(false, true, false, true), false, false) == STORY_CARD_NONE);
        assert(story_card_from(reel_is_clients(false, true, false, false), true, true) == STORY_CARD_HERS);
        assert(story_card_from(reel_is_clients(false, true, true, true), false, true) == STORY_CARD_AS_GIVEN);
    }

    test "on client work the prompt does not say the bot in speech is the house's" {
        assert(CLIENT_PROMPT_NO_HOUSE_BOT_NAME);
        assert(bot_named_in_speech(false));
        assert(!bot_named_in_speech(true));
    }

    test "VERSION says what the header's last note says" {
        assert(VERSION == 6);
    }
}

// phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY
